  "literature_notes": "All five ledger lines (L1\u2013L5) describe a single study (PMC3711070) in which MS4A6A was expressed as an EGFP-MS4A6A fusion using the pEGFP-C1 vector. In pEGFP-C1, EGFP is N-terminal to the cloned insert, placing the GFP tag at the intracellular N-terminus of MS4A6A (topology: residues 1\u201346 are intracellular). Critically, the fusion protein was NOT detected at the plasma membrane; it was retained intracellularly in the perinuclear trans-Golgi complex (co-localisation with giantin). Because the protein never reached the cell surface, this construct provides no evidence of a tolerated extracellular tag insertion. No other ledger lines exist for MS4A6A. The two extracellular loops (ECL1: 68\u201386; ECL2: 138\u2013185) are topologically available but are entirely unsupported by any ledger evidence of a tolerated insertion. Zero sites is the correct answer.",
